        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Rethrow mid-turn precheck signal",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- rethrow mid-turn precheck signals before persisting assistant failure messages\n- keep ordinary agent loop failures on the existing failure-message path\n\n## Why\n\nThe mid-turn tool-result precheck throws `MidTurnPrecheckSignal` so the embedded runner can compact and retry before the next model call. `CoreAgentHarness.executeTurn()` was catching every `runAgentLoop()` error and converting it into an assistant error message, so the outer attempt runner never observed the signal.\n\n## Validation\n\n- simplified the fix to one source file\n- confirmed compare shows one commit and one changed file: `packages/agent-core/src/harness/agent-harness.ts`\n- locally validated the name/message rethrow branch with a minimal Node reproduction\n- inspected OpenClaw 2026.5.28 session JSONL evidence showing mid-turn precheck errors persisted as assistant failures before compaction entries",
